# ML model weights/checkpoints — except the production regressors the
# worker actually loads at runtime (unlike the other checkpoints here,
# which are experiment artifacts, not load-bearing). `ml/models/*`, not
# `ml/models/` — excluding the directory itself means git never looks
# inside it, so a negation below can't re-include anything.
#
# regressor_v1.pt (terrain calibration, pipeline.py's CHECKPOINT_PATH) was
# missed when this carve-out was first added — same bug class as the two
# real production incidents this exact rule already caused: koppen.zip
# (silt jobs 404ing) and river_silt_regressor_xgb_v1.json itself (every
# silt job failing) — both fixed only after they broke in prod. Without
# this checkpoint, calibrate_scene() never runs and every terrain job
# silently falls back to relative_dsm regardless of SRTM availability.
ml/models/*
!ml/models/river_silt_regressor_xgb_v1.json
!ml/models/regressor_v1.pt
.cache/

# Derived sanity-test imagery and cached raster tiles (regenerable, keeps binary bloat out of git)
ml/depth/samples/
ml/data/samples/
ml/data/cache/

# Raw supplementary DEM/Sentinel-2 imagery staged locally for ml/data/
# ingest_supplementary.py — multi-GB rasters, never meant for git (see
# docs/open_decisions.md, 2026-08-30 supplementary-data entries).
/supplementary-data/
/_to_delete/
# Cargo.lock: commit it for binaries, gitignore it for libraries — see https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/faq.html#is-it-advisable-to-commit-cargo-lock-and-when
# Anchored to repo root — an unanchored "data/" pattern matches any dir
# named "data" at any depth, which silently shadowed both ml/data/ (source
# code) and frontend/src/data/ (validation_report.json, PRD §15/§20.2).
/data/

# Raw dataset downloads staged at repo root before being moved into /data/
/Train-Track1-RGB.zip
/Train-Track1-Truth.zip
/SWORD_v17b_shp.zip
/ml/data/river_silt_raw/sword/
/Track1-RGB/
/Track1-Truth/

# Manual-review diagnostic imagery (regenerable from real patches, not for git)
/review_samples/

# River silt use case: raw SSC matchup CSVs (multi-GB, external datasets),
# staged at repo root before being sorted into ml/data/river_silt_raw/.
# Except koppen/ — that's a small (2.7MB) reference table the pipeline
# actually reads at inference time (ml/features/koppen_climate.py), not
# training-only raw data. Real bug found 2026-09-17: it was never
# committed at all, so every georeferenced silt job failed in production
# with FileNotFoundError — this predates any dockerignore change, the file
# was simply never in the repo Northflank builds from.
# `/ml/data/river_silt_raw/*`, not the bare dir — excluding the directory
# itself would make the negation below unreachable (same gotcha as the
# ml/models/ fix above).
/*.csv
/ml/data/river_silt_raw/*
!/ml/data/river_silt_raw/koppen/
!/ml/data/river_silt_raw/koppen/Koeppen-Geiger-ASCII.txt

# GCP service-account key (Earth Engine credential) — root-only, never
# committed regardless of filename; nested json (package.json, tsconfig,
# manifest.json etc.) is untouched.
/*.json
